{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790258953,"nonce":"cAtSMO7IujuZRUL4+4QbXayj36U=","title":"os.exit and sys.exit drop output written without a trailing newline","message":"`io.write(\"a\") os.exit(3)` prints nothing on zylua (lua5.4 prints `a`), and `print(\"a\", end=\"\"); sys.exit(3)` prints nothing on zypy (python3 prints `a`). Both exit with the right status. The builtin `zb_exit` calls libc `exit`, which flushes C stdio but not Rust's line-buffered stdout, so a partial last line is lost. Same on main dea6d08b.\n\nReproducers:\n\n    -- lua\n    io.write(\"a\")\n    os.exit(3)\n\n    # python\n    import sys\n    print(\"a\", end=\"\")\n    sys.exit(3)\n\nNeeds a conformance case in each suite once fixed (lua5.4 / python3 produce `a`).","files":null}]}